<title>UK: Sullom Voe Brent terminal resumes berthings.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe Brent terminal resumes berthings.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Berthing resumed at the Sullom Voe Brent Blend crude oil terminal on the Shetland Islands early on Tuesday after a 48-hour suspension due to high winds, a port official said.</p>
<p>He said wind speeds dropped at 0400 GMT on Tuesday, allowing three tankers to come alongside to load two million barrels of crude.</p>
<p>&quot;There are three ships now loading... but the wind is forecast to blow up again tonight,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Private forecasters Weather Services Corp said west-southwest winds of 20-30 miles per hour (mph) in the North Sea would become southwesterly and increase to 25-50 mph on Wednesday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
</text>
